## View order

Large left: full-body elevated three-quarter view. Right column, top to bottom: intended front, side, rear. The middle view is side-like, but the sheet does not establish a rigorously true orthographic side. The front and rear are visually similar because the creature has no face.

## Visual QA and limitations

Both previews show a coherent low woody thorn shrub with visible muted moss-green foliage, secondary brown roots and branches, and large black thorn clusters. The core is concealed. No visible face, equipment, red accents, emissive effects, text, panel borders, or scenery. All four depictions fit in the landscape canvas with contact shadows on grey.

Anatomy remains unresolved: only three main leg shafts are clearly separable in the large view; another root/foot shape overlaps the right-side support. The corrective attempt did not achieve four independently countable corner legs with clear gaps. Small-view rear supports also overlap. Feet have multiple clawlike root tips rather than consistently simple two-way forks. This is a concept reference, not an approved anatomy turnaround.

Foliage is more finely textured than the requested broad, low-to-moderate-detail clumps, and some thorn highlights appear somewhat glossy. The camera angle and small creature scale are interpretations, not verified measurements. The palette reads green/brown/black, but no colour percentages or exact rendered HEX matches were measured. Cross-view clump and thorn placement is approximate rather than mechanically identical.

